# Remote dev is the live workspace

`https://dev.app.bokito.ai` runs from **`/opt/bokito-dev`** on the VPS (systemd hot reload). The laptop git checkout is **not** that runtime.

## When this workspace is local (Windows path, not `/opt/bokito-dev`)

1. **Prefer Cursor Remote-SSH** into host `bokito-dev`, folder `/opt/bokito-dev`, and edit there. That is the default for feature work.
2. If the session is still on the laptop checkout: after every meaningful code change that operators should see on dev, **sync those files to the VPS before saying the work is done**. Do not leave changes only local when the user is validating on `dev.app.bokito.ai`.
3. Sync over SSH host **`bokito-dev`** (or `root@31.97.45.44` with `$USERPROFILE\.ssh\hostinger_vps`). Target tree: `/opt/bokito-dev/...` matching repo paths.

### Safe sync pattern

- `scp` each file to `/tmp/...` with a **unique remote name** (never two sources named `auth.py` into the same folder — the second overwrites).
- On the VPS: `cp` into the correct `/opt/bokito-dev/...` path; `sed -i 's/\r$//'` on Python files.
- Schema changes: `cd /opt/bokito-dev/apps/api && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && ./.venv/bin/alembic upgrade head`.
- Worker-only code: `systemctl restart bokito-dev-worker`. API/dashboard usually reload themselves.
- Verify: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://127.0.0.1:8010/api/health` → `200`.

### Do not

- Assume laptop `npm run dev` / local uvicorn is what the user sees on `dev.app.bokito.ai`.
- Touch `/opt/bokito` (production/staging checkout) or prod compose for routine feature work.
- Commit or push solely to “get code onto dev” — hot-reload sync is enough; git remains for PR/master.

Full setup notes: `docs/DEPLOY.md` → **Remote dev**.
